@title "Mine pump: FSE'04's quantities, ASE'08's operations"

# Letier and van Lamsweerde, "Reasoning about Partial Goal Satisfaction for
# Requirements and Design Engineering", SIGSOFT'04/FSE-12, pp. 53-62
# (goal-controller#208), re-keyed from its text: §3.2 (heuristics H1-H3) and
# §3.3 (the PCTL patterns), the only places it prints the mine pump.
#
# The minimal seed: the five goals FSE'04 names, each with its words, and the
# one goal it quantifies, Achieve [WaterAlarmIffCriticalWaterLevel], with its
# two quality variables, its two objective functions (Min, targets 10^-4 and
# 10^-3) and their PCTL instances. The structural mine pump (operations,
# agents, interfaces) follows it, below the FSE'04 goals (#209).
#
# What FSE'04 doesn't print, so this seed doesn't have:
# - a refinement: the goals "contribute" to the Avoid goals (§3.2 H2, §4.3),
#   without the refinement being drawn;
# - an estimate of any quality variable, so no objective function has a
#   value (the targets are no results): kaossim reports both unresolved;
# - an objective function's name or target for the two Avoid goals (§3.2
#   describes them in words, kept as their definitions).
#
# The PCTL symbols are FSE'04's Wingdings glyphs as read: 0xA1 (pdftotext's
# "¡") is ○, next; 0xA8 ("¨") is □, globally ("the CTL symbols F (finally)
# and G (globally) are noted ◊ and □", §3.3). 10-4 is 10⁻⁴.

declare goal [ miner_in_overflowed_mine ]
  name "Avoid [MinerInOverflowedMine]"
  definition "The objective function for this goal is the conditional probability that a miner is in the mine when the mine is overflowed (FSE'04 §3.2, H2). §4.3 names it Avoid [MinerInsideOverflowedMine]: PumpOnWhenHighWater and AlarmWhenMineOverflowed contribute to it."
end

declare goal [ working_shift_lost ]
  name "Avoid [WorkingShiftLost]"
  definition "The objective function for this goal is to minimize the probability of losing an 8-hour working shift in order not to lose more than one shift in a thousand (FSE'04 §3.2, H2)."
end

declare goal [ water_alarm_iff_critical_water_level ]
  name "Achieve [WaterAlarmIffCriticalWaterLevel]"
  definition "The water alarm should be raised if, and only if, the water level exceeds the 'Overflow' limit."
  qualityvariable [WaterAlarmFailure] Boolean
  samplespace [WaterAlarmFailure] "set of all time points at which the water level becomes critical"
  qualitydefinition [WaterAlarmFailure] "WaterAlarmFailure is true if the alarm is not raised when the water level becomes critical. Its probability is the conditional probability that the alarm is not raised when the water level becomes critical."
  qualityvariable [FalseWaterAlarmInShift] Boolean
  samplespace [FalseWaterAlarmInShift] "set of all possible working shifts"
  qualitydefinition [FalseWaterAlarmInShift] "FalseWaterAlarmInShift is true if at some time during the working shift (8 hours) the water alarm is raised when the water level is not critical"
  objective [AlarmFailureRate] "WaterAlarmFailure"
  objectivespec [AlarmFailureRate] "WaterLevel ≥ 'Overflow' ⇒ Pr≥1−10⁻⁴ ○ WaterAlarm = 'On'"
  modal [AlarmFailureRate] Min
  target [AlarmFailureRate] 0.0001
  objective [FalseAlarmRate] "FalseWaterAlarmInShift"
  objectivespec [FalseAlarmRate] "Pr≥1−10⁻³ □≤8h (WaterAlarm = 'On' → WaterLevel ≥ 'Overflow')"
  modal [FalseAlarmRate] Min
  target [FalseAlarmRate] 0.001
end

declare goal [ pump_on_when_high_water ]
  name "PumpOnWhenHighWater"
  definition "FSE'04 §4.3: its quality variables and AlarmWhenMineOverflowed's are not independent, because the design used the same water sensor to detect high water levels, that would trigger the pump, and water levels that would raise the alarm in case of pump failure."
end

declare goal [ alarm_when_mine_overflowed ]
  name "AlarmWhenMineOverflowed"
  definition "FSE'04 §4.3: see PumpOnWhenHighWater."
end

# The operational layer (goal-controller#209): Letier, Kramer, Magee and
# Uchitel, "Deriving Event-Based Transition Systems from Goal-Oriented
# Requirements Models", ASE Journal 15(2), 2008 (ASE'08), §2 and §4, on
# Letier and van Lamsweerde's FSE'02 operation model (§2.1.4, §3, §4), re-keyed
# from their text (docs/papers/letier-fse02-icse02.md, §2.3-2.5 and §3.4-3.5):
# - the three requirements on PumpController (ASE'08 Fig. 2), their
#   FormalDef in KAOSTools' words: `[] (HighWater ∧ ¬Methane -> X PumpOn)` is
#   `when … then next …`;
# - PumpController's operations startPump and stopPump with their domain
#   and required conditions (Fig. 3), one operationalisation per
#   requirement, each set of ReqPre/ReqTrig for the requirement it names;
# - the environment's operations on the water level (§4, step 2: aboveHigh
#   as printed, belowHigh, aboveLow and belowLow "in a similar way") and on
#   methane (methaneAppears, methaneLeaves: their names are the paper's
#   fluent definition's, their conditions the step 2 rule's);
# - the state variables HighWater, LowWater, Methane and PumpOn as the Boolean
#   attributes of the objects they describe, LowWater initially true.
#
# The requirement's name is spelled three ways across the sources: Figure 2's,
# PumpOnWhenHighWaterAndNoMethane, the one it is declared with, is kept; the
# other two are packages/dialect/docs/reference-defects.md's (ASE'08).
# Nothing here is copied from the paper's models archive (no licence stated):
# kaoslts's FSP is compared with it by structure, in mine-pump-lts.expected.csv.

declare goal [ pump_on_when_high_water_and_no_methane ]
  name "Maintain [PumpOnWhenHighWaterAndNoMethane]"
  definition "If the water level is above high and there is no methane, then at the next time unit the pump must be on."
  formalspec when sump.highWater and not mine.methane then next pump.pumpOn
  assignedto pump_controller
end

declare goal [ pump_off_when_methane ]
  name "Maintain [PumpOffWhenMethane]"
  definition "If there is methane in the mine, the pump must be off within the next time unit."
  formalspec when mine.methane then next not pump.pumpOn
  assignedto pump_controller
end

declare goal [ pump_off_when_low_water ]
  name "Maintain [PumpOffWhenLowWater]"
  definition "If the water is below the low level, the pump must be off within the next time unit."
  formalspec when sump.lowWater then next not pump.pumpOn
  assignedto pump_controller
end

declare agent [ pump_controller ]
  name "PumpController"
  monitors sump.highWater, sump.lowWater, mine.methane
  controls pump.pumpOn
end

declare agent [ environment ]
  name "Environment"
  type environment
  controls sump.highWater, sump.lowWater, mine.methane
end

declare entity [ sump ]
  name "Sump"
  type environment
  attribute highWater : bool
  attribute lowWater : bool
  initially lowWater : true
end

declare entity [ mine ]
  name "Mine"
  type environment
  attribute methane : bool
end

declare entity [ pump ]
  name "Pump"
  type shared
  attribute pumpOn : bool
end

declare operation [ start_pump ]
  name "startPump"
  dompre not pump.pumpOn
  dompost pump.pumpOn
  performedby pump_controller
  input sump, mine
  output pump
  operationalizes pump_on_when_high_water_and_no_methane
  reqtrig [pump_on_when_high_water_and_no_methane] sump.highWater and not mine.methane
  operationalizes pump_off_when_methane
  reqpre [pump_off_when_methane] not mine.methane
  operationalizes pump_off_when_low_water
  reqpre [pump_off_when_low_water] not sump.lowWater
end

declare operation [ stop_pump ]
  name "stopPump"
  dompre pump.pumpOn
  dompost not pump.pumpOn
  performedby pump_controller
  input sump, mine
  output pump
  operationalizes pump_on_when_high_water_and_no_methane
  reqpre [pump_on_when_high_water_and_no_methane] not (sump.highWater and not mine.methane)
  operationalizes pump_off_when_methane
  reqtrig [pump_off_when_methane] mine.methane
  operationalizes pump_off_when_low_water
  reqtrig [pump_off_when_low_water] sump.lowWater
end

declare operation [ above_high ]
  name "aboveHigh"
  dompre not sump.highWater and not sump.lowWater
  dompost sump.highWater
  performedby environment
  output sump
end

declare operation [ below_high ]
  name "belowHigh"
  dompre sump.highWater
  dompost not sump.highWater
  performedby environment
  output sump
end

declare operation [ above_low ]
  name "aboveLow"
  dompre sump.lowWater
  dompost not sump.lowWater
  performedby environment
  output sump
end

declare operation [ below_low ]
  name "belowLow"
  dompre not sump.highWater and not sump.lowWater
  dompost sump.lowWater
  performedby environment
  output sump
end

declare operation [ methane_appears ]
  name "methaneAppears"
  dompre not mine.methane
  dompost mine.methane
  performedby environment
  output mine
end

declare operation [ methane_leaves ]
  name "methaneLeaves"
  dompre mine.methane
  dompost not mine.methane
  performedby environment
  output mine
end
